description:
Design a power-on reset (POR) circuit that generates a reset signal for a specified duration after system startup. On each rising edge of the clock, the circuit increments a 32-bit counter until it reaches a predefined limit (32'hffffff). While the counter is below this threshold, the reset output remains HIGH, indicating that the system should remain in a reset state. Once the counter exceeds the limit, the reset signal is deasserted to LOW, allowing normal operation to commence.
module top_module(
	input			clk,
	output	reg		rst
);

code:
module top_module(
	input			clk,
	output	reg		rst
);reg	[31:0]	counter;

always @(posedge clk) begin
	if (counter < 32'hffffff) begin
		rst <= 1;
		counter <= counter + 1;
	end
	else begin
		rst <= 0;
	end
end

endmodule

