Design a synchronous up-counter with a 4-bit output. The counter increments its output value on each rising edge of the clock signal (`clk`). A reset signal (`rst`) initializes the counter to zero when asserted. If the reset is not active, the counter continues to count up, wrapping around to zero after reaching its maximum count.
