description:
Design a digital circuit that counts the number of consecutive '1' bits in the least significant four bits of a 16-bit input signal. On each clock cycle, if the input signal is zero, reset the count to zero. If the input signal is all ones (16'hFFFF), set the count to four. The output will represent the count of consecutive '1's from the right side of the input, with a maximum value of four. This module effectively serves as a consecutive '1' counter for the specified input range.
