description:
Implement an unsigned 8-bit multiplier that produces a 16-bit product. The module takes two 8-bit inputs, `a` and `b`, and computes their product `p` using a combinational approach with a nested loop structure. It accumulates partial products in a 16-bit register `p_reg`, iterating through all combinations of bits from both input values, ensuring that the results fit within the 16-bit output size.
module top_module(
  input [7:0] a,
  input [7:0] b,
  output [15:0] p
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [7:0] a,
  input [7:0] b,
  output [15:0] p
);reg [7:0] a_reg;
  reg [15:0] p_reg;

  integer i, j;

  always @(*) begin
    a_reg = a;
    p_reg = 0;

    for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin
      for (j = 0; j < 8; j = j + 1) begin
        if ((i + j) < 16) begin
          p_reg[i + j] = p_reg[i + j] + a_reg[i] * b[j];
        end
      end
    end
  end

  assign p = p_reg;

endmodule

