description:
Design a 4-bit left shift circuit that takes a 4-bit input and shifts its bits to the left by one position. The most significant bit (MSB) is duplicated at the least significant bit (LSB) position, effectively preserving the sign bit for signed numbers. The output is a 4-bit result reflecting this left shift operation.
