description:
Design a circuit that calculates the average of a 25-bit input value, `val`, on the rising edge of the clock signal, `clk`. The module initializes an output register, `avg`, to zero and iterates through each bit of the input `val` to sum its values. The final result, which represents the sum of the bits in `val`, is stored in the output register `avg` after the clock edge. Note that this implementation does not perform a proper averaging by dividing the sum by 25; it simply outputs the total sum of the input bits.
