description:
Design a delay counter that generates a delay signal based on clock cycles. It initializes a 20-bit counter to a specific value (833334) on reset, and decrements this count with each clock cycle when enabled. The output `delay_enable` becomes high when the counter reaches zero, indicating that the specified delay period has elapsed. This module can be used in applications requiring precise timing control or delays in digital circuits.
module top_module(
	input clk, reset, enable,
	output delay_enable
);

code:
module top_module(
	input clk, reset, enable,
	output delay_enable
);reg [19:0] count;
	always @(posedge clk) begin
		if (!reset)
			count <= 20'd833334;
		else if (enable) begin
			if (count == 20'd0)
				count <= 20'd833334;
			else
				count <= count - 1'b1;
		end
	end

	assign delay_enable = (count == 20'd0) ? 1 : 0;endmodule

