description:
Design a reset synchronizer that stabilizes an asynchronous reset signal in a synchronous clock domain. The module takes an input reset and a clock signal, generating a synchronized output, rst_sync, that reflects the reset condition after two clock cycles. This two-stage flip-flop synchronizer ensures that any glitches or unexpected transitions on the reset signal are filtered out, providing a clean, stable reset output to downstream components in the design.
module top_module(
  input reset,
  input clk,
  output rst_sync
);

code:
module top_module(
  input reset,
  input clk,
  output rst_sync
);parameter n = 2; // number of cycles that reset must be stable

reg [1:0] sync_reset; // two-stage synchronizer

always @(posedge clk) begin
  sync_reset[0] <= reset;
  sync_reset[1] <= sync_reset[0];
end

assign rst_sync = sync_reset[1];

endmodule

