description:
Design a Manchester encoding circuit that generates two output signals based on the transitions of the input signal. The outputs, out1 and out2, toggle on each positive edge of the input, producing a differential signal: when the previous state is low (0), out1 is set high (1) and out2 low (0); conversely, when the previous state is high (1), out1 goes low (0) and out2 high (1). This implementation facilitates the encoding of binary data, useful for synchronous communication systems.
