description:
Design a reset control circuit that monitors the clock (CLK) and a reset request signal (reset_req). When reset_req is asserted, the circuit initializes a 9-bit counter and keeps the reset output active high. On each subsequent clock edge, if the counter reaches its maximum value, the circuit sets the reset output low. If the counter has not reached its maximum, it increments the counter and keeps the reset output active high. This design ensures that the system can be reset and transitions to a normal operation state based on the counter's status.
module top_module(
	input CLK,
	input reset_req,
	output reg reset = 1'b1
	);

code:
module top_module(
	input CLK,
	input reset_req,
	output reg reset = 1'b1
	);reg [8:0] counter = 9'b0;

always @(posedge CLK, posedge reset_req)
begin
	if(reset_req)
	begin
		counter <= 'b0;
		reset <= 1'b1;
	end
	else
	begin
		if(&counter)
		begin
			reset <= 1'b0;
		end
		else
		begin
			counter <= counter + 1;
			reset <= 1'b1;
		end
	end
end

endmodule

